  "Question": "Which of the following is not equal to \\(\\dfrac54?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac{10}{8}\\)",
    "B": "\\(1\\dfrac14\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\dfrac{3}{12}\\)",
    "D": "\\(1\\dfrac15\\)",
    "E": "\\(1\\dfrac{10}{40}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "First write \\(\\frac54=1\\frac14\\). Reducing the fractions in the choices gives\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{8}=\\frac54,\\qquad\n\\frac3{12}=\\frac14,\\qquad\n\\frac{10}{40}=\\frac14.\n\\]\nThus A, B, C, and E all equal \\(\\frac54\\). But \\(\\frac15<\\frac14\\), so \\(1\\frac15\\) is different. The answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
